# Keep the build context to what actually compiles.
#
# Docker honours this file, not .gitignore — so without it `COPY . .` sweeps in
# whatever is lying around the working tree. Two things make that more than an
# efficiency question here: backend/app.db is tracked in git, so a real database
# would be baked into a build layer, and .env holds JWT_SECRET and any API key.
# Neither reaches the final image (that stage copies only the binary), but both
# would sit in the build stage's cached layers.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# SQLite database plus its write-ahead log and shared-memory sidecars.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
Makefile
README.md
*.md
